From 37c2b382e0f75b8bd62f620cf3df3614f522e3ea Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ryan Kilroy <ryan.kilroy@n43studio.com>
Date: Sun, 12 Apr 2026 16:23:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 020/110] fix+feat: route MR beads to rig DB and add rig-prefix
 validation (gt-7y7, gt-gpy) (#3540)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

When a polecat works on a cross-rig bead (e.g., hq-xxx), bd.Create for
the MR bead resolved to the town-level database instead of the rig's
database. The refinery scans only its own database, so it never found
the MR and the branch sat unmerged indefinitely.

Fix: add Rig field to CreateOptions (passes --rig to bd create) and set
Rig: rigName when creating the MR bead in done.go and mq_submit.go.

Also add ValidateRigPrefix() to internal/beads/routes.go — a post-creation
guard that warns when a newly created bead's prefix doesn't match the
expected rig prefix. Applied (warning-only) at MR bead creation in done.go,
mq_submit.go, and conflict resolution task creation in refinery/engineer.go.

Also: auto-save uncommitted implementation work in done.go as a safety net.

Fix lint: listAllSlingContexts always returned nil error — remove error
return value and update all call sites. doMergePR had an unused ctx
parameter — remove it.

Co-authored-by: Claude Sonnet 4.6 <noreply@anthropic.com>
